<div class="rescue" data-temperature-rescue>
 <header><p class="eyebrow">TEMPERATURE RESCUE</p><h3>Restore five stations. Then choose the safe route.</h3><p>Every station checks a calculation and a model decision. There is no timer or penalty for revising.</p><strong data-progress aria-live="polite">0 of 5 stations restored</strong></header>
 <div class="stages">
  <fieldset data-stage="1"><legend><span>1</span> Signal Calibration · Represent</legend><p>An instrument is 6°C below zero. Translate the context, build −6 with exactly 12 chips, and find its opposite.</p><div class="fields five"><label>Signed integer<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="-6"/></label><label>Positive chips<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="3"/></label><label>Negative chips<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="9"/></label><label>Opposite<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="6"/></label><label>Context direction<select data-expected="below"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="above">Above zero</option><option value="below">Below zero</option></select></label></div><p class="model-note">Model target: 3P/9N → six negative chips remain → −6.</p><button type="button" data-stage-check>Restore station 1</button><p data-status role="status">Translate the context and complete the chip model.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-stage="2" disabled><legend><span>2</span> Chinook Tracker · Add</legend><p>Hourly changes are −7, +12, −4, +3. Predict the overall sign, record each running total, and verify the first cancellation.</p><div class="fields five"><label>Predicted sign<select data-expected="positive"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="negative">Negative</option><option value="positive">Positive</option><option value="zero">Zero</option></select></label><label>After −7<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="-7"/></label><label>Then +12<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="5"/></label><label>Then −4<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="1"/></label><label>Then +3<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="4"/></label></div><div class="fields"><label>Zero pairs in (−7)+(+12)<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="7"/></label><label>Remaining chip type<select data-expected="positive"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="negative">Negative</option><option value="positive">Positive</option></select></label></div><button type="button" data-stage-check>Restore station 2</button><p data-status role="status">Prediction, running totals, and chip cancellation must agree.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-stage="3" disabled><legend><span>3</span> Mountain Route · Number line</legend><p>Start −5 m. Move +13, −9, +6. Use a vertical line, record endpoints, and repair the faulty claim “the endpoints are +13, −9, +6.”</p><div class="fields five"><label>Start<input type="number" data-expected="-5"/></label><label>Endpoint 1<input type="number" data-expected="8"/></label><label>Endpoint 2<input type="number" data-expected="-1"/></label><label>Endpoint 3<input type="number" data-expected="5"/></label><label>Best orientation<select data-expected="vertical"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="horizontal">Horizontal only</option><option value="vertical">Vertical elevation line</option></select></label></div><label class="wide">Repair the claim<select data-expected="moves"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="moves">+13, −9, +6 are moves; +8, −1, +5 are endpoints</option><option value="correct">The claim is correct</option><option value="restart">Restart at zero each time</option></select></label><button type="button" data-stage-check>Restore station 3</button><p data-status role="status">The start, signed jumps, endpoints, and orientation must agree.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-stage="4" disabled><legend><span>4</span> Equipment Recovery · Subtract with tiles</legend><p>Model (+4)−(−7) and (−6)−(+5). Enter each result, the minimum zero-pair count, and the correct modelling order.</p><div class="fields four"><label>(+4)−(−7)<input type="number" data-expected="11"/></label><label>Pairs needed<input type="number" data-expected="7"/></label><label>(−6)−(+5)<input type="number" data-expected="-11"/></label><label>Pairs needed<input type="number" data-expected="5"/></label></div><label class="wide">Tile sequence<select data-expected="build"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="combine">Build both integers and combine</option><option value="build">Build the minuend, add complete zero pairs, remove the subtrahend</option><option value="unmatched">Add only the chip type being removed</option></select></label><button type="button" data-stage-check>Restore station 4</button><p data-status role="status">Use unsigned pair counts and preserve each minuend.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-stage="5" disabled><legend><span>5</span> Temperature Comparison · Change and distance</legend><p>Stations A=−17°C, B=−8°C, C=+2°C. Calculate directed changes and the nonnegative distance from A to C.</p><div class="fields four"><label>A→B<input type="number" data-expected="9"/></label><label>B→C<input type="number" data-expected="10"/></label><label>C→A<input type="number" data-expected="-19"/></label><label>Distance A/C<input type="number" data-expected="19"/></label></div><div class="fields"><label>Best model<select data-expected="line"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="chips">Thirty-five loose chips</option><option value="line">A labelled number line</option></select></label><label>Why is distance unsigned?<select data-expected="separation"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="direction">It describes direction</option><option value="separation">It describes nonnegative separation</option></select></label></div><button type="button" data-stage-check>Restore station 5</button><p data-status role="status">Directed changes keep signs; distance is nonnegative.</p></fieldset>
 </div>
 <section class="final" data-final hidden><p class="eyebrow">FINAL COMMAND DECISION</p><h3>Which plan satisfies both constraints?</h3><p>Include each starting temperature when finding the lowest temperature. A route must stay at or above −6°C and finish at least 0°C.</p><div class="plans"><article><strong>Plan North</strong><p>Start −6; changes +11, −8, +5</p></article><article><strong>Plan South</strong><p>Start +1; changes −4, +9, −7</p></article></div>
  <div class="route-evidence"><fieldset><legend>Plan North calculations</legend><div class="fields four"><label>Start<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="-6"/></label><label>Three directed changes<input data-sequence data-expected="11,-8,5" placeholder="+11, -8, +5"/></label><label>Successive endpoints<input data-sequence data-expected="5,-3,2" placeholder="+5, -3, +2"/></label><label>Lowest, including start<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="-6"/></label><label>Margin above −6<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="0"/></label><label>Final<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="2"/></label></div></fieldset><fieldset><legend>Plan South calculations</legend><div class="fields four"><label>Start<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="1"/></label><label>Three directed changes<input data-sequence data-expected="-4,9,-7" placeholder="-4, +9, -7"/></label><label>Successive endpoints<input data-sequence data-expected="-3,6,-1" placeholder="-3, +6, -1"/></label><label>Lowest, including start<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="-3"/></label><label>Margin above −6<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="3"/></label><label>Final<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="-1"/></label></div></fieldset></div>
  <label>Choose the valid plan<select data-final-plan data-expected="north"><option value="">Choose</option><option value="north">Plan North</option><option value="south">Plan South</option></select></label>
  <fieldset class="model-proof"><legend>Build two-model evidence</legend><p>Choose any valid starting chip model for −6. Equivalent models with added zero pairs are accepted. Then build the complete North route on a scaled number line.</p><div class="fields five"><label>Starting positive chips<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-chip-start-p/></label><label>Starting negative chips<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-chip-start-n/></label><label>Positive chips added<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="11"/></label><label>Zero pairs cancelled<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-chip-cancel/></label><label>Positive chips remaining<input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-expected="5"/></label><label>Chip result<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-expected="5"/></label></div><div class="fields"><label>Line start<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-start data-expected="-6"/></label><label>Jump 1<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-jump data-expected="11"/></label><label>Endpoint 1<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-end data-expected="5"/></label><label>Jump 2<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-jump data-expected="-8"/></label><label>Endpoint 2<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-end data-expected="-3"/></label><label>Jump 3<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-jump data-expected="5"/></label><label>Final endpoint<input class="signed-entry" inputmode="text" data-line-end data-expected="2"/></label></div><button type="button" data-build-final-line>Build and verify complete North line</button><div class="final-line" data-final-line role="img" aria-label="No final number line built yet."></div><p data-chip-status role="status">Build an equivalent chip model and the complete four-position North route.</p></fieldset>
  <label class="wide">Crew explanation<textarea rows="4" data-explanation placeholder="Explain why the verified lowest temperature, margin, and final temperature support your plan."></textarea></label><p class="review-note">Your calculations and model fields are checked automatically. Your explanation is recorded for self or teacher review, not judged by keywords or length.</p><button type="button" data-final-check>Send final command</button><p data-final-status role="status" tabindex="-1">Complete both routes, choose the plan, build two models, and record an explanation.</p>
 </section>
</div>
<script>
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-temperature-rescue]').forEach(root=>{
 let complete=0;const stages=[...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLFieldSetElement>('[data-stage]')],progress=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-progress]');
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[type="number"][data-expected]').forEach(input=>{const label=input.closest('label')?.textContent?.toLowerCase()||'';if(!/pair|chip|distance|margin/.test(label)){input.type='text';input.inputMode='text';input.classList.add('signed-entry');}});
 stages.forEach(stage=>{const legend=stage.querySelector<HTMLElement>('legend');if(legend)legend.tabIndex=-1;});
 const normalized=(value:string)=>value.replace(/\s+/g,'').replace(/\+/g,'');
 const wrongControl=(scope:HTMLElement)=>[...scope.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement|HTMLSelectElement>('[data-expected]')].find(control=>{if(control.value.trim()==='')return true;if(control.hasAttribute('data-sequence'))return normalized(control.value).replace(/−/g,'-')!==normalized(control.dataset.expected||'').replace(/−/g,'-');if(control instanceof HTMLInputElement){const raw=control.value.trim().replace('−','-');if(control.classList.contains('signed-entry'))return !/^[+\-]?\d+$/.test(raw)||Number(raw)!==Number(control.dataset.expected);if(control.type==='number')return Number(control.value)!==Number(control.dataset.expected);}return control.value!==control.dataset.expected;});
 stages.forEach((stage,index)=>stage.querySelector('[data-stage-check]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const wrong=wrongControl(stage),status=stage.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]');if(wrong){if(status)status.innerHTML='<strong>Not restored yet.</strong> Recheck the focused translation, calculation, or model choice.';wrong.focus();return;}stage.dataset.complete='true';stage.classList.add('complete');if(status)status.innerHTML='<strong>Station restored.</strong> Every required value and model decision is verified.';complete=Math.max(complete,index+1);if(progress)progress.textContent=`${complete} of 5 stations restored`;if(stages[index+1]){stages[index+1].disabled=false;stages[index+1].querySelector<HTMLElement>('legend')?.focus({preventScroll:true});stages[index+1].scrollIntoView({behavior:matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches?'auto':'smooth',block:'center'});}else{const final=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final]');if(final){final.hidden=false;final.querySelector<HTMLElement>('h3')?.setAttribute('tabindex','-1');final.querySelector<HTMLElement>('h3')?.focus({preventScroll:true});final.scrollIntoView({behavior:matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches?'auto':'smooth',block:'start'});}}}));
 stages.forEach((stage,index)=>stage.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement|HTMLSelectElement>('input,select').forEach(control=>{const invalidateStage=()=>{if(stage.dataset.complete==='true'){delete stage.dataset.complete;stage.classList.remove('complete');const status=stage.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]');if(status)status.textContent='Answer changed. Restore this station again; later evidence must be rechecked.';for(let i=index+1;i<stages.length;i++){stages[i].disabled=true;delete stages[i].dataset.complete;stages[i].classList.remove('complete');}const final=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final]');if(final){final.hidden=true;const finalStatus=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final-status]');if(finalStatus)finalStatus.textContent='Earlier station changed. Restore the route before sending a final command.';}complete=index;if(progress)progress.textContent=`${complete} of 5 stations restored`;}};control.addEventListener('input',invalidateStage);control.addEventListener('change',invalidateStage);}));
 root.querySelector('[data-build-final-line]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const start=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-line-start]'),jumps=[...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-line-jump]')],ends=[...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-line-end]')],values=[start,...jumps,...ends].map(x=>Number((x?.value||'').replace('−','-'))),ok=values.join(',')==='-6,11,-8,5,5,-3,2',line=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final-line]');root.dataset.finalLineVerified=String(ok);if(line){const points=[-6,5,-3,2],pct=(n:number)=>(n+10)/20*100,ticks=Array.from({length:21},(_,i)=>`<i style="--p:${i*5}%"><b>${i%5===0?i-10:''}</b></i>`).join(''),arrows=[[points[0],points[1],11],[points[1],points[2],-8],[points[2],points[3],5]].map((x,i)=>`<span class="route-arrow" style="--from:${pct(x[0])}%;--to:${pct(x[1])}%;--level:${i}"></span><em style="--p:${(pct(x[0])+pct(x[1]))/2}%;--level:${i}">${x[2]>0?'+':''}${x[2]}</em>`).join('');line.innerHTML=ok?`<div class="rescue-line">${ticks}${arrows}${points.map((x,i)=>`<span class="route-point ${i===0?'start':i===3?'final':'middle'}" style="--p:${pct(x)}%"></span>`).join('')}</div><p>Start −6; +11 to +5; −8 to −3; +5 to +2.</p>`:'<p>Revise the start, all three jumps, and every endpoint before building the line.</p>';line.setAttribute('aria-label',ok?'Scaled number line from negative ten to positive ten. Start negative six; jump positive eleven to positive five; jump negative eight to negative three; jump positive five to positive two.':'Final route is not yet valid.');}});
 root.querySelector('[data-final-check]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const final=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final]')!,wrong=wrongControl(final),explanation=root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('[data-explanation]'),status=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final-status]');if(wrong){if(status)status.innerHTML='<strong>Revise.</strong> Recheck the focused route value, plan choice, or model field.';wrong.focus();return;}if(root.dataset.finalLineVerified!=='true'){if(status)status.innerHTML='<strong>Build the complete number line.</strong> Verify all three jumps and four positions.';root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-build-final-line]')?.focus();return;}if(!explanation?.value.trim()){if(status)status.innerHTML='<strong>Record your explanation.</strong> It will be saved for review without keyword or length scoring.';explanation?.focus();return;}root.dataset.finalComplete='true';if(status)status.innerHTML='<strong>Rescue complete.</strong> Plan North has endpoints +5, −3, +2; its lowest temperature including the start is −6°C, its safety margin is 0°C, and it finishes at +2°C. Plan South’s values are also verified. Equivalent chip evidence and the complete multi-jump line are valid; the explanation is recorded for review.';status?.focus({preventScroll:true});});
 root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final]')?.querySelectorAll('input,select,textarea').forEach(control=>control.addEventListener('input',()=>{delete root.dataset.finalComplete;if(!(control instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement))delete root.dataset.finalLineVerified;const status=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final-status]');if(status)status.textContent=control instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement?'Explanation changed. Send the final command again to record it.':'Final mathematical evidence changed. Rebuild the line and send the final command again.';}));
 root.addEventListener('click',event=>{const button=(event.target as HTMLElement).closest('[data-final-check]');if(!button)return;const p=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-chip-start-p]'),n=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-chip-start-n]'),cancel=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-chip-cancel]'),chipStatus=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-chip-status]');const pv=Number(p?.value),nv=Number(n?.value),cv=Number(cancel?.value),valid=!!p?.value&&!!n?.value&&!!cancel?.value&&pv>=0&&nv>=0&&pv-nv===-6&&cv===Math.min(nv,pv+11)&&pv+11-cv===5&&nv-cv===0;if(!valid){event.preventDefault();event.stopImmediatePropagation();if(chipStatus)chipStatus.innerHTML='<strong>Revise the chip model.</strong> Start with any nonnegative counts whose value is −6. Add 11 positives, cancel every available zero pair, and leave 5 positives.';(p?.value===''?p:n?.value===''?n:cancel)?.focus();return;}if(chipStatus)chipStatus.innerHTML='<strong>Equivalent chip model verified.</strong> The starting model equals −6 and the +11 change leaves +5.';},true);
});
</script>
<style>
.rescue{border-radius:17px;overflow:hidden;background:#0b2635;color:#fff}.rescue>header{padding:1.25rem;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0b2635,#14536d)}.rescue>header h3{margin:.2rem 0;font-size:1.55rem}.rescue>header>[data-progress]{display:inline-block;padding:.55rem .75rem;border-radius:9px;background:#ffffff18}.stages{display:grid;gap:1px;background:#ffffff24}.stages fieldset{margin:0;padding:1rem;border:0;background:#f6fbfd;color:#172738}.stages fieldset[disabled]{opacity:.62;background:#e8eef1}.stages fieldset.complete{border-left:7px solid #218b52}.stages legend,.route-evidence legend,.model-proof legend{display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:center;font-weight:900}.stages legend span{display:grid;place-items:center;width:2rem;height:2rem;border-radius:50%;background:#14536d;color:#fff}.fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem}.fields.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}.fields.five{grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr))}.fields label,.wide,.final>label{display:grid;gap:.35rem;font-weight:800}.fields input,.fields select,.wide textarea,.wide select,.final>label select{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:inherit;min-height:44px;padding:.65rem;border:1px solid #78909c;border-radius:9px;background:#fff}.stages button,.final>button{margin-top:.8rem;border:0;border-radius:9px;padding:.7rem .9rem;background:#176b77;color:#fff;font-weight:900;min-height:44px}.stages [data-status],.final [data-final-status],.model-note{padding:.65rem;border-radius:8px;background:#fff}.final{padding:1.2rem}.plans,.route-evidence{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem;margin:.8rem 0}.plans article,.route-evidence fieldset{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid #ffffff38;border-radius:10px;background:#ffffff12}.route-evidence .fields{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.model-proof{display:grid;gap:.75rem;margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #ffffff45;border-radius:11px}.final [data-final-status],.review-note{color:#172738;background:#fff;padding:.7rem;border-radius:8px}.rescue button:focus-visible,.rescue input:focus-visible,.rescue select:focus-visible,.rescue textarea:focus-visible,.rescue legend:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #f5c451;outline-offset:2px}@media(max-width:900px){.fields.five{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.fields.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:780px){.rescue>header{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:2}.fields,.fields.four,.fields.five,.plans,.route-evidence,.route-evidence .fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}.stages button,.final>button{width:100%}}@media(max-width:390px){.stages fieldset,.final{padding:.75rem}.rescue{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.fields input,.fields select,.wide textarea,.wide select{max-width:100%}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{scroll-behavior:auto!important;transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}
</style>
<style>
@media(max-width:390px){.rescue>header{position:static}.model-proof,.route-evidence fieldset{min-width:0}.rescue input,.rescue select,.rescue textarea,.rescue button{font-size:1rem;min-height:44px}}
.final-line{padding:.8rem;border-radius:9px;background:#fff;color:#172738}.rescue-line{position:relative;height:130px;margin:3.5rem .8rem 0;border-top:3px solid #263447}.rescue-line i{position:absolute;left:var(--p);top:-7px;width:1px;height:13px;background:#263447}.rescue-line i b{position:absolute;top:14px;transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:.72rem}.route-arrow{position:absolute;left:min(var(--from),var(--to));width:calc(max(var(--from),var(--to)) - min(var(--from),var(--to)));top:calc(-28px - var(--level)*17px);border-top:5px solid #d76a20}.rescue-line em{position:absolute;left:var(--p);top:calc(-50px - var(--level)*17px);transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:.75rem;color:#8b3e0e}.route-point{position:absolute;left:var(--p);top:-12px;width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);background:#7a4ba3;border:2px solid #fff;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #7a4ba3}.route-point.start{background:#2457c5;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #2457c5}.route-point.final{background:#d76a20;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #d76a20}@media(max-width:390px){.rescue-line{transform:scale(.82);transform-origin:left center;width:120%}}
</style>
